t it, which is very improbable.  \n\nReason: Playing the pair of Ks maximizes control and minimizes risk of the Landlord winning. It blocks the Landlord from playing their last card if it\'s a single, and since my teammate has only 2 cards, they can likely finish after I play this pair. Passing is not allowed in Free Play, and playing a low card could give the Landlord a chance to win. Thus, ♠K ♣K is the best move.  \n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠K", "♣K"]}'}
